# text_id = 1584
# text = A second telegram seated that a catch of four boats of 28,000 mackerel had been thrown overboard by the Newlyn fishermen , that the boats were not allowed to go to sea , that Cornishmen were in full possession of the boats , that the authorities were helpless , and that 16 Yarmouth and Lowestoft boats were in the harbour .
