# text_id = 1593
# text = He strongly supported the Trades Unions in some things , but he was sorry to notice that the more modern tendency of Trades Unionism was to support arrangements which tended to keep employers and workmen at arms length , rather than to encourage arrangements such as that proposed in the Amendment which had the effect of bringing them amicably together .
