# text_id = 1757
# text = The honourable Gentleman desires , as I understand , to discuss on the Report of Supply not merely the negotiations in China with regard to concessions of railways , but also the general question as to whether Parliament should itself incur pecuniary liability in regard to railways not in British territory , for it is only in regard to that question that Lord Salisbury referred to the House of Commons .
