# text_id = 1761
# text = Bat I contend that the Bill of 1884 was not put forward as a settlement or as a complete measure , but merely as the best measure that was possible in the circumstances , and I fail to see how it is possible to reasonably or logically regard the Motion of the right hon . Gentleman the Member Halifax as any other than an effort to complete the work of 1884 .
