# text_id = 1763
# text = If , as a matter of course , British officers who entertain foreign officers are to be recouped their outlay , the act of hospitality would be regarded as losing much of its grace and spontaniety ; and to give a general permission to naval officers to entertain those of other countries would not be in accordance with the traditions of the Service or the means of the Exchequer .
