# text_id = 1768
# text = In view of the very serious accidents which occurred almost constantly , it was of the utmost importance that the House and the country should realise that here was a great opportunity for the Government to give compensation for them ; but the Government were afraid to extend what they maintained was to be a great boon to the working classes , to the largest class of labourers in the country .
