# text_id = 1775
# text = As to the funds out of which arrears are to be paid and provisions to be made for impoverished tenants in stocking farms and rebuilding cottages which have been destroyed , the hon . Member who moved the Second Reading , said , they were perfectly willing to revert to the proposal of the Bill which I introduced — namely , to throw the cost on a purely Irish fund .
