# text_id = 1779
# text = The foundation being gone , what was the use of trying to prop up the superstructure ; Established Churches , as they survived among us now , were but a pale and feeble shadow of what they had been four centuries ago , free , no doubt , from the worst faults that had then deformed them , but without that solid basis on which they then stood firm .
