# text_id = 1780
# text = On the ground of protecting administration , and to keep local authorities out of the difficulties and trouble arising out of action on reports issued upon inadequate knowledge , he believed the best thing to do would be to cut out the reference to sanitary inspectors for this duty for which they had not been trained and which in the present state of the law they were not qualified to perform .
