# text_id = 1785
# text = On behalf of the hon . Member for East Tipperary , Mr. T. J. CONDON , I beg to ask the Secretary to the Treasury , as representing the Postmaster - General , whether he is aware of the great inconvenience suffered by people of Cahir , Clonmel , and Carrick - on - Suir arising from the frequent and long delays in the arrival of the morning mails from Dublin .
