# text_id = 1786
# text = SIR J. GORST hoped that in the long discussions which they would have on this Bill , Members of the Committee would not mistake brevity on his part for discourtesy ; he was most desirous of treating every suggestion made by the Committee with proper consideration — [ " hear , hear ! " ] — but he should endeavour to make his remarks as terse and brief as he could .
