# text_id = 1791
# text = I see no other solution but in opening up the country by railroads and canals , encouraging private enterprise to develop the native resources of India , and notably the practically untouched mineral wealth of the country , attracting capital from this country to multiply and augment the great stable industries of India , and associating with this policy of industrial development a more technical and utilitarian system of education .
