# text_id = 1803
# text = Under regulations of long standing a Sunday post can only be established in a rural district on receipt of a memorial signed by the recipients of not less than two - thirds of the correspondence for the places affected , and in the present instance it is found from returns taken that the memorialists receive about one - fifth only of the correspondence for the Roserea and Clonakenny post .
