# text_id = 1836
# text = There is at present , I believe , an Army clothing factory in Ireland , and as you have only a War Office in London and not in Dublin or in Ireland , it has been the custom from the time when this Army clothing factory was established in that country , to have sent up from Limerick specimens of the clothing to Pimlico before it was accepted or approved of .
