# text_id = 1842
# text = I consider that if the old Whig maxim were true that taxation without representation is tyranny , then the converse is also true that representation without taxation is also tyranny , and it is to avoid that state of things that I intend to support the Amendment of my hon . Friend , which declares that the present excessive representation of Ireland in this House should be put an end to .
