# text_id = 1864
# text = THE EARL OF MEATH rose to move the Second Reading of this Bill , the object of which , he explained , was to add to and extend the scope of the Museums and Gymnasiums Act , 1891 , and also to extend to provincial County Councils the powers at present possessed by the London County Council and a large number of urban sanitary authorities throughout England and Ireland .
