# text = If the Chancellor of the Exchequer was right , that only implied that there was something wrong in the scheme ; in other words , it must be obvious that , if there was to be injustice or oppression owing to the Amendment not being adopted , the proposals of the Bill must be at fault , and graduation , equalisation , and simplification were being sought in a wrong way .
