# text_id = 1874
# text = Leases were , therefore , destroyed ; the essence of them was struck out by the Act of 1881 , and all we did by the Act of 1887 was to carry out to its logical issue the process which had been begun , and put an end to a state of things which could not be justified , as far as I know , on any principle whatever .
