# text_id = 1876
# text = SIR R. WEBSTER said , that from the Government Memorandum , he gathered that the mere arrangement whereby a life interest was to be given by a wife to a husband or a husband to a wife was not to be regarded as belonging to that class of settlement by which property was so tied up that it was necessary for extra duty to be paid in respect of it .
