# text_id = 1883
# text = The Bill only imposed this one restriction on the full rights of the landlord — that where the landlord turned out a tenant without fair and just cause , or refused to renew the tenancy , or to grant reasonable conditions of tenure , the tenant should be able to claim under the ordinary principles of compensation a fair allowance for the loss which he had to face owing to removal .
