# text_id = 1898
# text = MR. SWIFT MACNEILL said , he would obey exactly in the spirit and the letter everything the Speaker bade him ; but he would like to point out that every one of the Clauses in this Bill to which they ( the Nationalists ) objected on principle were proposed upstairs in Committee on the Municipal Franchise Bill , by Mr. John Ross , the defeated candidate for Derry , and rejected .
