# text_id = 1901
# text = We pointed out that the arrangement involved the collection of the instalments from the purchasing by agents of an Irish Government , entirely dependent on Irish public opinion , and that , in the event of the tenants being unable or unwilling to pay , the Irish Government would have thrown upon it the duty of imposing taxation in order to make good the default of the purchasing tenants .
