# text_id = 1903
# text = School committees had been going on for generations without any marked complaint being made to the Education Department , and although some further requirements were anticipated when the Free Education Act was passed , a year or so of gradual progress elapsed after its passage , and it was not until the present Government came into Office that demands were urged with what he regarded as exceptional and abnormal vigour .
