# text_id = 1915
# text = The Prime Minister ought to form his judgment , as he does now , on the Report of the Ministers responsible , but to bring him into close and constant communication with the War Office and the Admiralty would interfere with the ordinary duties of the Head of the Government , and prevent him from obtaining the acquaintance he ought to have with the views of the other Departments .
