# text_id = 1916
# text = He fully admitted that the powers of the Charity Commission required alteration , but he was sure the Chancellor of the Exchequer would admit that to attempt seriously to deal with a Bill of that kind , which would largely increase the powers of the Charity Commission , would be adding to such an extent to the already heavy load he had to curry that it would really break his back .
