# text_id = 1918
# text = I notice that the Government are prepared to show the greatest possible trust in the Irish people where the interests of the Irish Loyalists alone are concerned , but when they want cash — what an Irish farmer once said was bona fides , not only do they preserve the collection to their own officers , but they will not oven trust the Irish Courts with the duty of enforcing payment .
