# text_id = 1927
# text = It was a matter of common knowledge that Sir H. Robinson became , during his period of office at the Cape , deeply interested in commercial speculations at the Cape ; that those commercial speculations were initiated and promoted by the Prime Minister of the Cape Colony , and that the introduction of the High Commissioner to those speculations was owing to the action of the Prime Minister of Cape Colony .
